    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660-a1">

                <pb facs="1060" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg964"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No 887.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Count Maffei.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 24,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Count</hi>: I conveyed to my Government the
                    intimation you kindly gave me, that if a request were made by the President
                    through the diplomatic channel, leave would be granted to you to take charge of
                    the effects of this legation, if an occasion should arise to ask your good
                    offices in that regard.</p>
                <p>In reply I am informed that my Government has sent such a communication to that
                    of His Majesty the King of Italy.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to acquaint me with the further instruction you may receive on
                    this subject, and I in turn shall not fail to give you timely notice of my
                    movements.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
